AUTOCYCLE_REVIEW: <one JSON object as specified below>

AUTOCYCLE_REVIEW must contain:
- work_id and attempt_id: echo the controller work.id and attempt.id in AUTOCYCLE_WORK_CONTEXT; use "NONE" when absent. Never invent a replacement identity to escape unresolved work.
- finding_key: the stable underlying finding, retaining the current work's key while unresolved.
- blocking: JSON true only for concrete consequences preventing the current major-Step Completion or safe execution/verification; unrelated improvements are advisory. blocking_reason: the concrete consequence, otherwise "NONE".
- Evaluate the major Step Completion in the same IMPLEMENTATION.md. COMPLETE means the parent Completion is achieved and closes the entire major, including all continuation sub-steps. Sub-steps have no independent Completion. Only Review closes work; Cursor results are evidence.
- When AUTOCYCLE_WORK_CONTEXT has no checkpointed attempt, this is a valid opening Review, including after restart. Return outcome "UNASSESSED", reason "no checkpointed attempt exists to assess.", and evidence []; do not judge historical implementation as progress in this Session or invent a blocker from the absence of an attempt. Historical files can inform the new Plan and, when still applicable, the Session Endpoint assessment; they are not new attempt progress.
- An attempt with kind "planning" preserves a Plan blocker candidate, not implementation progress. Return outcome "UNASSESSED" and adjudicate the candidate against current repository evidence through REVIEW_STATUS and NEXT_STEP. Missing same-Session implementation evidence cannot block the first implementation attempt.
- outcome: "UNASSESSED" when no checkpointed attempt exists or the attempt is kind "planning"; for implementation attempts, "VERIFIED" for material change in evidence relevant to the parent Completion, "COMPLETE" for verified achievement of that Completion, "NONE" for no material progress, or "UNKNOWN" when evidence is insufficient. For legacy plans without Completion, inspect the original bounded work until Plan establishes Completion without reinterpreting that work.
- reason: explain how the actual checkpointed result relates to the parent Completion. If unsatisfied, judge whether to keep pursuing it: reconsider the approach or a distinct bounded continuation; if the evidence shows the intermediate goal is inappropriate, use reviewed defer_work; material evidence can reveal a wrong route too. AUTOCYCLE_WORK_CONTEXT.stagnation is the advisory count of consecutive reviewed bounded attempts without material progress toward this Completion. NONE adds one for that attempt; VERIFIED or COMPLETE resets it. Re-review, resume, interruption, planning or a blocker candidate alone do not add attempts. UNKNOWN is not a no-progress judgment. Use the count to reconsider the approach and major-Step relevance, never as a threshold, ceiling, score, percentage or automatic decision. You judge progress; Cursor and Plan do not set the count. A commit, changed file, new test, rewritten status, changed ID or regenerated artifact alone is never progress. Documentation and investigation count when they satisfy the actual objective.
- evidence: a JSON array of objects with path, sha256 (the actual current file SHA-256), and observation (the concrete test/measurement/result relevant to the original criterion). VERIFIED and COMPLETE require evidence you actually inspected. Paths must be in the repository or its AutoCycle evidence directory. Evidence can be a test log, structured metrics or the actual document/artifact; do not invent paths or hashes. Do not modify files to create evidence during Review.
- Historical work may satisfy part of the Session Endpoint without being new progress in this attempt. AUTOCYCLE_WORK_CONTEXT.prior_reviews provides locators from retained reports (including earlier Sessions), not proof or inherited acceptance. Use their plan/checkpoint revisions to locate the original scope and factual evidence. Never cite work-state, a cached Review, or another derived acceptance summary as factual evidence.
- To reuse a prior factual reference in evidence or endpoint.evidence, inspect the underlying file and retain its path and original sha256; add prior_attempt_id from the locator and applies_to: [{"path":"current relevant artifact or input","sha256":"hash bound by the historical facts","observation":"what this binding establishes"}]. Include all relevant source/input/artifact bindings, grounded in the historical receipt, snapshot or tested revision, not freshly chosen hashes of changed files. Explain in observation why the original check still establishes the CURRENT requirement, considering intervening changes, dependencies, environment and freshness. The controller checks referenced bytes, applicability hashes and revision ancestry; these checks alone do not establish semantic sufficiency.
- Reuse unchanged, still-applicable facts without rerunning their producer. A previous COMPLETE/VERIFIED decision, an unchanged log, or commit ancestry alone is insufficient. Missing, changed, stale, failed or inapplicable facts cannot inherit acceptance. If applicability cannot be established, report the remaining semantic uncertainty through UNKNOWN/unresolved_facts or an actual blocking finding; do not claim Endpoint REACHED. Inspect current artifacts directly when they prove the requirement independently of historical acceptance. Historical evidence supports Endpoint acceptance separately from current-attempt progress.
- When required evidence for the current parent Completion is missing and work remains blocking, return REVIEW_STATUS PROBLEMS (BLOCKED only with evidenced external dependency) and outcome UNKNOWN (UNASSESSED only when no checkpointed implementation attempt exists). Never use VERIFIED or COMPLETE with nonempty unresolved_facts, even if other partial progress is proven. Preserve that partial evidence and the genuine blockers; endpoint.status remains UNREACHED.
- Review owns semantic truth. Identify the actual fact required by parent Completion / Session Endpoint, decide materiality, and combine all admissible applicable evidence. Multiple authenticated native page observations may establish whole-document readability; no bespoke whole-document or aggregate receipt is required. Provenance is not an additional product criterion.
- State remaining material semantic uncertainty in unresolved_facts: [{"fact":"exact semantic uncertainty", "material_reason":"why current Completion or Endpoint requires it"}]. Use [] for established, immaterial or obsolete facts. Never create fact: "unclassified". Legacy unclassified state is context for fresh ordinary Review, never an execution task or a requirement to retain an obsolete evidence method.
- Legacy observation associations in AUTOCYCLE_WORK_CONTEXT.legacy_observation_review are historical provenance, not a current verdict. Inspect applicable evidence; do not treat rejected captures as new observations. If needed, request a supported read-only observation in this same Review. Never emit retry_observations or observation_recovery_id.
- missing_evidence is not a Review output channel; omit it or use []. Plan chooses the smallest finite supported route for unresolved_facts; the AutoCycle Controller validates executability before Implement. If no supported finite route exists, the Controller stops with a verification-capability gap, not recurring project work. Do not invent a verifier or require AutoCycle repairs as project acceptance.
- Inspect actual receipt outputs and applicable observations, not only producer status, request IDs, hashes, timestamps or ancestry. Generic producer JSON cannot establish an arbitrary semantic claim merely by matching requirement text. FAILED describes an execution result; UNAVAILABLE is not a recurring missing_evidence obligation. Real evidenced external dependencies retain existing BLOCKED behavior.
- Reuse admissible evidence when relevant artifacts, inputs, dependencies and environment remain applicable. A later Review boundary or timestamp alone never invalidates evidence. Require fresh observations for changed relevant inputs, independently changing conditions, or an explicit current-observation acceptance criterion. Reject stale or inapplicable observations. Include hash-bound applicability references in applies_to when reusing observations.
