- recovery: "NONE" normally. If blocked, "NEW_EVIDENCE" requires verified progress backed by newly inspected evidence; "REVISED_APPROACH" requires explicit new human instructions authorizing a concrete different approach, with recovery_instruction_ids drawn from new_instruction_ids and a concrete recovery_reason. Mere reruns or unrelated new instructions do not clear a block.
- recovery_instruction_ids: [] unless using REVISED_APPROACH. recovery_reason: "NONE" unless recovering.
If verification_only is true, this is the read-only progress recheck. Do not repair the progress mechanism. Unresolved verification requires PROBLEMS for bounded diagnosis; only evidenced external dependency permits BLOCKED.
Without SESSION.md, DONE requires current-work COMPLETE when an attempt exists. With a Session, first assess the current major Completion. Once achieved, close the entire major and evaluate the Session Endpoint. A verified already-satisfied Endpoint can also end a Session when no current major exists. Never falsely report unfinished work COMPLETE. Only opening Review judges Endpoint completion from the actual checkpointed state and SESSION.md, never merely Cursor success. When SESSION.md exists, report its Endpoint assessment each Review, but do not claim REACHED while the active major Completion remains unsatisfied: include endpoint: {"status":"REACHED|UNREACHED","session_sha256":"actual SESSION.md SHA-256","evidence":[objects with path, sha256, observation]}. REACHED requires inspected evidence of all Endpoint acceptance and MUST return DONE unless frozen instructions are PENDING incorporation; in that case return PASS/PROBLEMS and let Plan persist their changes before evaluating completion again. TARGET may remain unfinished. UNREACHED must not return DONE. Without SESSION.md retain legacy all-TARGET completion semantics. Unused cycles never justify more work. For a fresh session (flag 1), return PASS/PROBLEMS to derive the new Endpoint and Priority from TARGET, current project state and supplied instructions and replan; never accept the previous session Endpoint.
PROBLEMS with blocking=false records advisory findings; Plan should select the highest-priority authorized objective, not a recursive administrative repair.
PROMPT_EOF
    PROMPT=${PROMPT%$'\n'}

    local BASE_PROMPT="$PROMPT" BASE_LOG="$REVIEW_LOG"
    local REVIEW_ATTEMPT VALIDATION_FAILURE PROGRESS_SUMMARY
