Persistence and planning discipline:
- TARGET.md is the project destination. SESSION.md holds this session Endpoint and Priority. IMPLEMENTATION.md holds only current bounded work.
- During Review classify each undelivered instruction by actual effect: target, endpoint, priority, implementation; a request can affect several levels. Classify every ID still needing incorporation, using implementation for concrete execution guidance; never reuse delivered IDs. For independently satisfied inputs (INPUT_STATUS COMPLETE), use an empty direction object and do not request document changes. Record direction as a JSON object mapping those levels to exact instruction IDs in AUTOCYCLE_REVIEW. Plan follows those bindings through the existing instruction mechanism.
- If an explicit Target, Endpoint or Priority amendment makes unresolved work irrelevant, Review may include defer_work: {"work_id":"current work.id","instruction_ids":["authorizing direction instruction IDs"],"reason":"why the amendment defers this work relative to the Endpoint"}. Preserve its original plan and evidence in the ledger; deferral is not completion and cannot clear a missing-evidence block. Review may also use defer_work with empty instruction_ids after outcome NONE or VERIFIED when the evidence shows the intermediate goal is no longer a sensible route to the Session Endpoint; give the concrete relevance reason. Difficulty alone does not justify replacement. Plan may start a different major only after closure or this reviewed deferral; do not carry deferred ancestry into IMPLEMENTATION.md.
- Target changes never invent a new Endpoint. Reconcile the existing Session and report an actual conflict for a human decision. Priority-only changes leave TARGET unchanged; technique-only changes leave TARGET and SESSION unchanged.
- Endpoint and Priority persist until explicitly changed; record their changes in SESSION.md, never only in queue receipts. On an ordinary start or explicit --restart, derive a new Endpoint and Priority from TARGET, current project state and any supplied instruction. Otherwise preserve legacy work without inventing an Endpoint; normal --instruct can establish it.
- Before selecting any increment ask: "Does this materially advance the current SESSION Endpoint or unblock something required to reach it?" If no, defer it.
- Prefer the smallest direct change that can achieve the current Completion, end-to-end product capability, demonstrated current needs, reuse, and bounded repairs. Leave adequate working subsystems alone. Among valid steps choose the largest meaningful user-visible or product-level progress toward the Endpoint, governed by Priority.
- New abstractions, frameworks, compatibility machinery, hypothetical edge-case hardening and cleanup are justified only by the current Endpoint, a demonstrated defect, two or more concrete present uses, or safety/correctness of the direct implementation. Elegance alone is insufficient.
- Blocker candidates are evidence to adjudicate as a real blocker, bounded repair, or deferred work; do not recursively redesign neighboring systems.
Read existing IMPLEMENTATION.md, SESSION.md, TARGET.md, and directly relevant files only as needed.

Rules:
- One bounded implementation step.
- Review can authorize bounded technical repair and expansion of machine-generated file restrictions within the existing user-authorized goal. It cannot override explicit user constraints, permissions or access controls; TARGET changes require explicit user instruction.
- Preserve the parent work identity and Completion until Review closes it or explicitly defers an inappropriate intermediate goal. A new major introduces a new Completion. A distinct continuation changes its bounded implementation objective and keeps the parent Completion; simply continuing the same attempt keeps its ID.
- Preserve unfinished commitments and still-applicable constraints from the current plan, including its AUTOCYCLE_PLAN.inputs commitments. Carry these into the new plan until satisfied or explicitly superseded; do not restart completed one-time actions. Record remaining scope when an input requires more than this bounded step.
- Missing evidence must not be invented; human decisions and unavailable access remain blockers.
- When the current work is absent or provisional, inherited IMPLEMENTATION.md is context, not an admitted current-Session attempt requiring progress or closure. Plan the first bounded implementation from current repository state, preserving applicable user constraints and unfinished obligations.
- For each Review unresolved_facts entry, preserve its exact fact and criterion. Add evidence_routes to AUTOCYCLE_PLAN: [{"fact":"the unchanged Review fact", "evidence":[existing {path,sha256,observation,applies_to} references], "commands":[["existing executable","existing check script","args"]], "requests":[existing Office Bridge request objects]}]. Omit unused lists. Respect Session Priority and dependencies; a low-level blocker does not automatically outrank useful endpoint work. Prefer applicable existing evidence, then a finite set of supported inspections/checks/tests/captures, then a product change only for an actual defect. Commands must use installed executables and existing project checks; never invent a verifier or create AutoCycle infrastructure. Native captures/navigation go through Office Bridge, not arbitrary Office shell commands. Plan's finite request/command lists are execution instructions, never a new acceptance standard.
- When no finite supported route exists, emit a normal plan block retaining the parent Completion and include evidence_routes: [{"fact":"exact Review fact","missing_capability":"specific missing AutoCycle mechanism; explain why no finite supported route could be constructed"}]. The Controller will stop before publishing or Implement with a verification-capability gap. Do not use PLAN_STATUS BLOCKED for capability absence or turn it into an implementation objective.
- If no authorized bounded plan is possible, output PLAN_STATUS: BLOCKED followed by BLOCKER: <concrete reason>, without a plan block. This is a candidate for read-only Review, not a final decision.
- Cursor must never modify TARGET.md, SESSION.md or IMPLEMENTATION.md.
- Direct completion records and measured verification to RESULT.md.
- Read RESULT.md when assessing the previous step.
- Follow Review's Completion-relative blocker adjudication: defer irrelevant candidates; repair only what directly prevents the unchanged Completion; use a distinct continuation only when warranted; select a new major only after reviewed closure or deferral of the wrong route. Do not independently treat Cursor's candidate as a blocker or change Completion to escape difficulty. Preserve ownership and recovery guards. Record advisory findings and choose the highest-priority remaining authorized work. Numbering or wording alone cannot demand another implementation cycle.
- Preserve useful project-specific naming/conventions.
- The only required bounded-work criterion is one concise ## Completion statement in IMPLEMENTATION.md. It belongs to the major Step, never SESSION.md or a sub-step. Beyond this statement, choose the amount of detail the work needs; no fixed template, acceptance criteria, checklist, tests, evidence prescription or Done when section is required. Optional acceptance guidance and mandatory checks remain ordinary plan content. Cursor chooses reasonable verification unless you explicitly require a check.
- Omit rationale, history, repetition, and obvious instructions.
- Aim for no more than about 60 lines.
- Do not implement, modify files, commit, or push.
- No Markdown fences.

Output ONLY:

BEGIN_IMPLEMENTATION_MD
<complete IMPLEMENTATION.md with a concise objective heading and whatever prose detail the bounded work needs.
Only when undelivered instructions exist, include one line AUTOCYCLE_PLAN: {"inputs":[{"id":"exact instruction ID","commitment":"concrete incorporation and remaining scope"}]}. Include every undelivered ID exactly once; this is the existing delivery receipt, not an acceptance schema.
An optional AUTOCYCLE_PLAN record may specify minor: 1 for the first distinct continuation after Review of the initial major attempt, then minor: 2, etc. Initial major work has no minor; omit minor to continue the same bounded attempt. The controller stamps IDs and identity metadata. Do not manufacture acceptance fields.>
END_IMPLEMENTATION_MD
For explicitly instructed changes authorized by Review direction, append BEGIN_TARGET_MD / END_TARGET_MD and/or BEGIN_SESSION_MD / END_SESSION_MD blocks with the entire corresponding Markdown document. Omit unchanged documents. SESSION.md stays small: optional Session: ${AUTOCYCLE_SESSION_NUMBER:-1}, ## Endpoint, optional acceptance bullets, ## Priority. Preserve sections not explicitly changed.
For a fresh session (${AUTOCYCLE_NEW_SESSION:-0}), a new SESSION block and fresh bounded work are required. Derive Endpoint and Priority from TARGET.md, current project state and supplied instructions; no Endpoint instruction is required. TARGET persists unchanged unless explicitly instructed. Never start a new Session automatically after completion.
PROMPT_EOF
    PROMPT=${PROMPT%$'\n'}

    set +e
    printf '%s' "$PROMPT" |
        adjudication run "${AUTOCYCLE_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT:-900}" codex exec --sandbox read-only --output-last-message "$ANSWER" - \
        >"$PLAN_LOG" 2>&1
    EXIT_CODE=$?
    set -e

